# The factory release whose FPGA design a MODERN release carries in its BOOT.bin.
# Decided 2026-09-30 (.planning/decisions/after-issue-9.md): a modern (v2.x)
# release ships a BOOT.bin, built from exactly this XSA, so one download boots a
# blank card and its bitstream traces back to a published, built-from-source
# factory release.
#
# Changing the FPGA design of the next v2.x is a one-commit change HERE, after a
# factory release exists to point at. sha256 is of that release's system_top.xsa
# asset; firmware-modern/fetch-pinned-xsa.sh and release.yml both refuse a
# mismatch.
#
# NOTE: v1.7's design is OLDER than main's (main's XSA md5 4d85a5aa is unreleased).
# A v2.x built from this pin carries v1.7's FPGA, not what main builds.
tag=v1.7
sha256=47f831009eb19b21a97a8136472d663e32a32cc42a5c26ba5e17f72d4f8f7e0b
